<title>USA: U.S. Stockpile to sell surplus bauxite.</title>
<headline>U.S. Stockpile to sell surplus bauxite.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Defense National Stockpile Center announced Thursday it would begin selling metalurgical grade bauxite, Surinam type, in January.</p>
<p>The agency said it would sell up to 300,000 long dry tons in negotiated, long-term contracts.</p>
<p>The first sale will be held at 1500 EST/2000 GMT on January 28.</p>
<p>-- Washington Commodities Desk (202) 898-8489</p>
</text>
